1,99,100,101,999,1000,12345,-1,-9,-10,-12345,INT_MAX,INT_MIN` + 256 random `i32` ⇒ returned C string compared byte-for-byte (and the pointer must be stable across calls) | [x] |\n| 67 | `sh_geti` | `num` in `0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8,12,13,16,17,24,32,33,64,100,257,1000` — stdout captured in a subprocess and compared byte-for-byte, plus exit status | [x] |\n| 68 | `sh_geti` | `num` negative / `INT_MIN` (all loops skipped) — subprocess stdout + status | [x] |\n| 69 | `seed` + `sh_geti` | `stbds_rand_seed(s)` before `sh_geti(num)` for `s` in `{0, 1, 7, 0xdeadbeef, SIZE_MAX}` × `num` in `{8, 33}` ⇒ different probe orders ⇒ different print order; must match | [x] |\n| 70 | `sh_geti` | called twice in the same process (global `stbds_hash_seed` has evolved) ⇒ second call's output differs from the first; must match C | [x] |\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false}}
