{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_yk7au27el6k6vup5xs6rpy7qlmyfy6gnvn45d755rndicypzv5uq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. **The Rust translation was already byte-identical to the C — no divergences were found and no fixes to `src/` were needed.**\n\n## What the library is\n`c_src/src/lib.c` is an amalgamation of `stb_ds.h` plus its `sh_geti` test driver. The public header exposes only `void sh_geti(int)`, but the `.so` exports **16** symbols (the whole `stbds_*` API), so all 16 were verified.\n\n## Phase A — artifacts (all created, all machine-checked)\n| file | content |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` | 16/16 symbols present in both `.so`s; the 9 `static` C symbols documented as intentionally private; imports confirmed libc-only |\n| `ERRORS.md` | **63 rows**, all `[x]` — every `STBDS_ASSERT`, every `return -1/0/NULL/a` early-out, every limit constant, plus G1–G6 generic FFI boundaries |\n| `CONFIGS.md` | **70 rows + 5 extras**, all `[x]`, with a machine-verified row→test mapping |\n\n`Cargo.toml` has **no `[features]`** and `CMakeLists.txt` has no build options ⇒ exactly one configuration. I verified it under **both** cargo profiles anyway, since `dev` adds integer-overflow and UB checks the C lacks.\n\n## Phases B–D — results\n- **114 tests**, all green in **release and debug** (228 runs). Every test loads *both* `.so`s via `libloading` and calls only exported symbols — no direct crate linkage.\n- Comparison is a full byte-level snapshot after **every** operation: array header, all 8 `hash`/`index` entries of every bucket, all 11 `stbds_hash_index` bookkeeping fields (incl. the evolving `seed`), arena `remaining`/`block`/chain, and every element's bytes.\n- Fatal rows (SIGSEGV/SIGABRT) are compared as **subprocess signal + byte-identical stdout**; `sh_geti`'s `printf` output likewise.\n- Symbol diff reaches **empty** for both profiles.\n\n## Harness validated by mutation testing\nEight deliberate bugs were injected into `src/` one at a time; **all eight were caught**, including the subtlest C quirks: the `int`-promotion sign-extension in the SipHash main loop and in tail `case 4`, and the stb bug where `stbds_hmput_key`'s wrap-around probe loop omits the `stbds_temp_key` update.\n\n## Three things that are *not* comparable (documented, excluded)\n1. `stbds_hash_index::temp_key` — never initialized by `stbds_make_hash_index`; compared only where a string put defines it.\n2. Element bytes `[keysize..elemsize)` after a put — `stbds_hmput_key` only `memcpy`s the key; the `hmput` macro stores the value, so tests do too.\n3. `realloc` capacity slack, and pointer identity/movement across two independent heaps.\n\nEvery earlier red test traced to one of these or to a wrong expectation of mine (e.g. I assumed `sh_geti`'s output was hash-ordered — it is insertion-ordered and therefore seed-independent), never to the translation. `c_src/` source files are untouched (only the cmake `build/` dir was added)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1865,"cache_read_input_tokens":352502,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1865,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0e5425a4-8ecc-4378-9224-5d24c05e87b1","uuid":"35198a55-9a46-4a03-9b66-8984afab81a6","timestamp":"2026-08-20T15:36:54.083Z"}
